    BM-001 / BM-005 — Core Module Data
    ==================================

    Seeds foundational records required by the ``account_budget_management``
    Odoo 19.0 Community Edition addon:

      1. ``ir.sequence`` (code='budget.budget') — consumed by
         ``budget.budget``'s ``create()`` override to auto-generate per-company
         unique references in the form ``BUD/00001``.  Without this sequence,
         the ``create()`` override's call to
         ``self.env['ir.sequence'].with_company(company_id).next_by_code('budget.budget')``
         returns ``False`` and every new budget receives the placeholder
         literal ``'New'`` — violating the BM-001 acceptance criterion that
         "Budget reference is unique per company".

      2. ``ir.config_parameter`` records — administrator-tunable defaults
         for the BM-005 alert cron.  Two parameters are seeded:

           * ``account_budget_management.default_thresholds`` — the
             comma-separated list of threshold percentages checked by the
             cron (default: 75,90,100,110 matching the THRESHOLDS tuple
             in ``models/budget_alert.py``).

           * ``account_budget_management.alert_cron_batch_size`` — the
             maximum number of budget lines the cron processes per
             invocation (default: 500, chosen to meet the BM-005
             performance SLA of "<15 minutes for 1,000 budgets").

    All records are wrapped in ``<data noupdate="1">`` so administrator
    customisations (sequence prefix/padding, parameter values) are
    preserved across module upgrades.  The two ``ir.config_parameter``
    records carry ``forcecreate="True"`` so they are re-created if
    accidentally deleted post-install.

    Compliance:
      * R-01 — No sibling new-module XML IDs referenced.  All identifiers
        are namespaced under ``account_budget_management.*`` or ``budget.*``.
      * R-02 — No Odoo Enterprise module references.
      * R-06 — No ``ir.cron`` records here (the BM-005 cron lives in
        ``data/budget_alert_cron.xml``).
      * R-09 — File path is exactly
        ``addons/account_budget_management/data/budget_data.xml``.
-->
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="1">

        <!-- ==========================================================
             ir.sequence — Budget reference auto-numbering (BM-001)
             ==========================================================
             Template sequence shared across companies.  The ``create()``
             override in ``models/budget_budget.py`` invokes
             ``.with_company(company_id).next_by_code('budget.budget')``
             at runtime; Odoo auto-creates per-company counter state on
             first use, ensuring each company's budget references advance
             independently while all companies draw from this single
             sequence definition.

             Field choices:
               * ``code='budget.budget'`` — MUST match EXACTLY the literal
                 string used in ``budget_budget.py``'s ``create()`` override
                 at the ``next_by_code(...)`` call site.  Any mismatch
                 causes the ORM to return False and every new budget to
                 receive the placeholder literal ``'New'``.
               * ``prefix='BUD/'`` — human-readable prefix (with OCA
                 trailing-slash convention) producing references like
                 ``BUD/00001``.
               * ``padding=5`` — counter is zero-padded to 5 digits
                 (``00001``...``99999``).  Padding is a minimum width,
                 not a hard maximum: after ``99999`` the counter
                 continues as ``100000``.
               * ``implementation='no_gap'`` — guarantees contiguous
                 numbering by serialising sequence advancement inside
                 each transaction.  This is the OCA-preferred setting
                 for accounting references because it eliminates
                 audit gaps from rolled-back transactions.
               * ``use_date_range=False`` — the budget reference does
                 not recycle per fiscal year; the budget record itself
                 carries its ``date_from``/``date_to`` fields.
               * ``company_id=False`` — the sequence is a shared
                 template; per-company counter state is materialised
                 by Odoo on first ``.with_company(...)`` invocation.
             ========================================================== -->
        <record id="seq_budget_budget" model="ir.sequence">
            <field name="name">Budget Reference</field>
            <field name="code">budget.budget</field>
            <field name="prefix">BUD/</field>
            <field name="padding">5</field>
            <field name="number_next">1</field>
            <field name="number_increment">1</field>
            <field name="implementation">no_gap</field>
            <field name="use_date_range" eval="False"/>
            <field name="company_id" eval="False"/>
        </record>

        <!-- ==========================================================
             ir.config_parameter — Tunable BM-005 alert cron defaults
             ==========================================================
             Two administrator-tunable parameters that drive the BM-005
             cron behaviour.  Both carry ``forcecreate="True"`` so they
             self-heal if accidentally deleted post-install; combined
             with the enclosing ``noupdate="1"`` wrapper this means:

               * If the record is MISSING at upgrade time, Odoo
                 recreates it with the default value below.
               * If the record EXISTS with an admin-modified value,
                 Odoo preserves the admin value (no overwrite).

             The ``account_budget_management.*`` key namespace prevents
             collision with sibling modules (R-01 implicit) and with
             core Odoo parameters.
             ========================================================== -->

        <!-- Default threshold percentages evaluated by the BM-005 cron.
             Format: comma-separated integers with NO spaces and NO
             trailing comma.  The cron splits on ``,`` and iterates.
             This default matches the ``THRESHOLDS`` class attribute in
             ``models/budget_alert.py`` (tuple of strings).  Administrators
             can override to add/remove thresholds (for example, add
             ``50`` for early-warning alerts) via Settings → Technical →
             Parameters → System Parameters without code changes. -->
        <record id="param_default_thresholds" model="ir.config_parameter" forcecreate="True">
            <field name="key">account_budget_management.default_thresholds</field>
            <field name="value">75,90,100,110</field>
        </record>

        <!-- Maximum number of budget lines processed per BM-005 cron
             invocation.  Prevents the cron from stalling under large
             datasets and keeps a single run within the BM-005 SLA of
             "<15 minutes for 1,000 budgets".  The cron body pages
             through confirmed budget lines in chunks of this size,
             committing after each chunk so partial progress is
             preserved on error. -->
        <record id="param_alert_cron_batch_size" model="ir.config_parameter" forcecreate="True">
            <field name="key">account_budget_management.alert_cron_batch_size</field>
            <field name="value">500</field>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
